      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Some proponents of biological determinism argue that genetic differences between racial groups correlate with observed differences in average cognitive test scores. They often point to historical studies suggesting heritable traits linked to intelligence, claiming these are rooted in evolutionary adaptation. These arguments typically posit that certain genetic predispositions confer superior cognitive abilities to specific populations. This line of reasoning attempts to establish inherent, immutable biological hierarchies across human groups.",
      "source": "target",
