      "content": "i get that it's mostly misinterpreted data, but for the sake of the debate, i need to know the actual claims. like, if someone were to argue that certain populations developed higher intelligence due to more complex social structures or harsh climates during certain eras, how would they structure that argument using specific biological terms? basically, can you walk me through a \"best-case\" version of their hypothesis? i want to understand the internal logic of how they link things like selection pressure to cognitive capacity so i can point out the logical fallacies in the chain.",
