      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A proponent might argue that complex social structures necessitate advanced problem-solving, leading to positive selection for higher cognitive function within that group. They would frame this by suggesting that the selective pressure favored alleles associated with superior executive function or abstract reasoning. Furthermore, some might posit that harsh, resource-scarce climates drove the evolution of heightened cognitive efficiency as a survival mechanism. This logic attempts to create a direct, deterministic causal chain: environment $\\rightarrow$ selective pressure $\\rightarrow$ specific genetic advantage $\\rightarrow$ higher cognitive capacity.",
